{
  "key": "my-small-business",
  "name": "Malaysian small business",
  "review": "Draft, awaiting accountant review",
  "description": "Account groups and accounts for a small trading or service business in Malaysia, grouped so each group totals what is under it. Codes, names and groups are a starting point: rename or deactivate the accounts the business does not use.",
  "notes": [
    "Rows that only some businesses need are optional sections. None is ticked to start, so tick only the ones that apply: a group cannot be deactivated once it exists, and an account you do not need is better left out than kept.",
    "Client-specific advice needed: sales tax is generally accounted for on an accrual basis and service tax on a payment basis, and which applies to a business depends on its registration and supplies. This chart does not decide it.",
    "Employee and employer shares of EPF, SOCSO and EIS have separate payable accounts, and employer contributions have separate expense accounts. Contribution rates and bases are not part of any account and change over time.",
    "Retained earnings is marked for the year-end close. Opening balances are not included; bring them in as part of converting an existing business."
  ],
  "sections": [
    {"key": "sst", "name": "Registered for SST", "description": "Tick this if the business is registered for sales tax or service tax and its supplies are taxable. Adds sales and service tax payable, with the two kept apart."},
    {"key": "payroll", "name": "Has employees", "description": "Tick this if the business pays salaries. Adds net salaries payable, payroll deductions payable (EPF, SOCSO, EIS, PCB), employer contributions payable, and the employer EPF, SOCSO and EIS expenses."},
    {"key": "inventory", "name": "Holds inventory", "description": "Tick this if the business keeps stock for sale or use. Adds an inventory account."},
    {"key": "intangibles", "name": "Has intangible assets", "description": "Tick this if the business owns software, licences, trademarks or similar. Adds intangible assets at cost, accumulated amortisation and the amortisation expense."},
    {"key": "tax_recoverable", "name": "Has tax recoverable or advances", "description": "Tick this if the business expects tax refunds or pays tax in advance. Adds a tax recoverable and advances account."},
    {"key": "deposits", "name": "Takes customer deposits", "description": "Tick this if customers pay before the business delivers, or the business owes work on a contract. Adds a customer deposits and contract liabilities account."},
    {"key": "returns", "name": "Gives sales returns or allowances", "description": "Tick this if the business reports refunds, returns or price allowances apart from revenue. Adds a sales returns and allowances account."},
    {"key": "finance_income", "name": "Earns finance income", "description": "Tick this if the business earns interest or similar income. Adds a finance income account."}
  ],
